+## v0.15.5 — the host pair moves to DeepSeek Harness 0.2.1-rc.3 + dsh-tui 0.17.0, and a README table says which pair each release was verified on
+
+Patch release over v0.15.4. A pin-and-documents wave: **no plugin behaviour changed**. The bundle now
+pins DeepSeek Harness **0.2.1-rc.3** and dsh-tui **0.17.0** — the pair whose declared peer bands admit
+each other — and the README finally states that correspondence in one table, in both languages.
+
+**Changed — the host pair is now 0.2.1-rc.3 + 0.17.0.** The three `@deepseek-ai/dsh-experimental-*`
+dependencies (`agent-team`, `client-ui-agent-team`, `tool-agent-team`) move to `0.2.1-rc.3`, and
+`bun.lock` is regenerated from the repo root with the pinned `bun@1.4.0`; `dsh-plugin.json`
+`compat.hosts` and the `host-tui` ref in `dsh-distribution.json` move to `0.17.0`. The atomicity is the
+point: 0.17.0's own peer ranges extend to `0.2.1-rc.3` (36 of its 39 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` peers append
+it), while 0.16.1 never declared rc.3, so the two bumps cannot be split. **No compatibility fix was
+owed**, and none was made: measured against the published artifacts, the rc.2→rc.3 umbrella is
+byte-identical under `lib/` and the sampled `.js` files and `.d.ts` surfaces this bundle binds are
+identical, while dsh-tui 0.17.0 keeps all fifteen `tui*` seam declarations and the
+`registry-0.15.json` profile byte-identical. That is why `manifestVersion`/`$schema` stay `0.15` and
+the adapter's version gates (`PANEL_CSV_HOST_OWNED_SINCE = "0.16.1"`,
+`PANEL_CSV_SELF_HEAL_SINCE = "0.15.0"`) and their fixtures did NOT move: those record WHEN the host
+changed behaviour, not which host is current.
+
+**Added — the README version-correspondence table.** `README.md` and `README.zh-CN.md` both carry one
+table right after Install: the release, the DeepSeek Harness it was built and verified against, and its
+DSH-TUI row — six releases from 0.14.0 through 0.15.5, every cell read from its release tag
+(`git show v<release>:package.json`, `dsh-plugin.json`'s `compat`, `dsh-distribution.json`'s `host-tui`),
+not inferred. The section also says where the two pins live (`package.json` for the harness,
+`dsh-plugin.json` `compat.hosts` + `dsh-distribution.json` for the TUI) and that a newer host is not
+claimed until a release row names it.
+
+**Changed — the Docker and QA carriers follow the pair.** Both Docker lanes, the UI stack, the four
+`presets/mpd.patch.yml` comments, `docker/README.md` + zh-CN and the `skills/dsh-qa` TUI carriers (the
+host-spec default and every `npm i -g …` remedy) now name `0.17.0` / `0.2.1-rc.3`, so a lane run
+tomorrow installs the pair this release pins. Historical measurements — the 0.16.1 peer-band
+statements, `docs/tui-dag-renderer.md`'s declaration reads, the `>= 0.16.1` range statements and every
+dated 2026 measurement — are deliberately left as history.
+
+**Changed — docs.** `AGENTS.md` §8, `docs/user-guide.md` + zh-CN, `docs/development.md` + zh-CN,
+`docs/tui.md` + zh-CN (preamble, plus the new §11.10 amendment for this wave), and the two README
+badges now name the new pair. `@dsh-std/sdk` stays at `0.1.1-rc.2`: it is a separate community line,
+not part of this host pair.
+
+**Fixed — stale prose the pin bump invalidated.** A comment-only pass over the claim sites this wave
+falsified, so a reader is never told a version this release does not pin: the docblock above
+`PANEL_CSV_HOST_OWNED_SINCE` in `packages/mpd-tui-adapter-plugin` now separates the two facts it had
+merged — 0.16.1 is the release that INTRODUCED host ownership (a permanent gate floor, so the constant
+never moves), while the ADMITTED host is declared in `dsh-plugin.json` `compat.hosts` (0.17.0 since this
+release); `packages/mpd-tui-plugin/README.md` + zh-CN move their "adapted to" target to `0.17.0`; and
+`packages/mpd-better-sidebar-host/README.md` + zh-CN move their current-pin literal to `0.2.1-rc.3`. The
+module header of `packages/mpd-better-sidebar-host/src/index.ts` stops naming a pin literal in its
+`connection` rationale and states the policy instead — the row mounts wherever the host's peer floor
+(`0.2.1-rc.1+`) and this bundle's own pin both admit the installed harness — so a later bump cannot make
+it false. No constant, fixture, test, exported symbol or behaviour moved, and
+`node scripts/verify-dist-fresh.ts` proves the comment-only edits leave every committed `packages/*/dist`
+byte-identical to a fresh build (33/33 targets fresh, each rebuilt twice).
